<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Sydney wheat futures face price pressure.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Sydney wheat futures face price pressure.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sydney wheat futures came under pressure in light trading on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The January 1997 contract dipped by A$1.00 to settle at A$163.00 a tonne. March, May and November were also down.</p>
<p>The trend lower ran counter to overnight gains in the CBOT wheat trding, where the market gained in part on perceptions that recent selling was overdone.</p>
<p>Local traders, however, reacted more to Monday's A$10.00 a tonne cut in its 1996/97 pool price estimate for Australian Standard White wheat to A$195.00 a tonne.</p>
